url: "https://github.com/LineBreaker30113/the-acs-project"
abstract: >-
  The Arity Component System (ACS) is an academic research project investigating
  the convergence of Polyadic Formal Concept Analysis (FCA), dynamically
  composable database architectures, and neuro-symbolic reasoning. Developed as an
  experimental research testbed for high-reasoning Retrieval-Augmented Generation
  (RAG), ACS models knowledge by structuring entities—such as factual
  paragraphs—across mathematical relations for PFCA reasoning, underpinned by
  well-defined procedures for verifiable information processing. To explore how
  autonomous agents reason over evolving knowledge, ACS introduces a live runtime
  class-loading mechanism that allows agents to safely synthesize, execute, and
  verify procedures while the database serves queries. The project formally
  investigates the fundamental trade-off between raw transaction latency and dynamic
  composability, serving as a formal laboratory for autonomous knowledge graph
  synthesis, request-level citation auditing, and lattice-based topological
  retrieval.
